serve these  materials and then provide them to  the public so  in the meantime we do in fact do some  some basic research although that  um  typically comes secondary to  that mission that i spoke of  so in terms of hemp  we're really trying to catch up on lost  time  this is a project that  should have been  in place for 70 years  so i'm trying to very rapidly bring this  germplasm collection up to speed with  for example the tomato collection or the  apple collection which we also keep here  um so what that looks like is initially  i'm trying to understand the  genetic and geographical diversity of  the broader pool of hemp germplasm we  have a lot of pieces of information  i've done a lot of work trying to  assemble them together build a database  of literature  online resources interviews with hemp  readers in other countries  um  assemble that all together  to help me gain a more comprehensive  picture of the broader pool of hemp  germplasm  secondly  i formed a number of really vital  collaborations  um to assist in this project so  my role will be primarily to  collect increase characterize and  distribute these materials  which will be made available on the  gren global  portal online which is an online  database that allows users to query  germplasm  and make requests so this tool also  allows us to collect and aggregate  large amounts of phenotypic or trait  data  so  these collaborations that i formed  will  leverage  capabilities in other areas to collect  and screen these materials that we'll be  collecting and distributing so for  example  i've been working closely with a lab  that characterizes cotton and flax fiber  i can send them materials from artwork  they can characterize it for fiber  traits  i will take that data and add it to the  grin global database  to make it publicly available  i formed  additional collaborations with  analytical labs that will be  characterizing secondary plant  metabolites  as well as working with some  groups  where 