nd researchers to  simply compare phenotypic traits across  genetically and geographically diverse  germplasm i think would be a great value  to the hemp community and i've been  really excited to  speak to the real experts  get their thoughts get their opinions  pull information out of papers compare  them side by side and assemble this hemp  descriptor's manual and ultimately i  hope that that information will be used  to  develop very specific mapping  populations that allow us to tease apart  the  genetic foundations of  key  hemp  horticulture agronomic traits  so  work that i see long term in the future  i would love to  gain a deeper understanding of this  wider pool of hemp genetic diversity  and work with many collaborators to  build that into a hemp magic population  that segregates for  many critical traits and captures the  the larger pool of hemp diversity i  think that would be  an enormously valuable resource that i'd  love to offer to  public and private plant breeders as  well as those working to map plant  traits  so as far as what the future holds  first and foremost i just want to add  more  diverse hemp genetic materials to our  collection while collecting as much  phenotypic data to accompany those  materials at the same time so that's  kind of goal number one is just to scale  build  um  our collection  i would also like to improve our ability  to produce a lot of high quality seed  hemp is  a very challenging crop it's dioecious  it's wind pollinated so a lot of our  typical  greenhouse  seed increase procedures are not  applicable in the same way pollen  control is of vital importance  so developing methods to  handle those challenges  will be  ongoing  project i'm also really interested in  developing new collaborations and  partnerships  um i i think it's exciting that hemp is  such a diverse crop that's applicable to  so many different  industries and groups and stakeholders  that i'd love to  help harness the power of hemp's  incredible 